historical_business_count":8},{"category":"Nightlife","historical_business_count":5},{"category":"Bars","historical_business_count":5}],"history":[{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","review_id":"gzkjzBKOj-9BGZf445jKAA","date":"2013-09-29T00:31:11","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9443262815475464,"text_excerpt":"I love this place. Yes, there's smoke, but I've never found it oppressive (and I hate smoke). The selection is lovely, and I love that you can get an \"English\" pint, which just makes my night better with that extra 4oz of delicious per serving. The atmosphere is SO laid back. The bartenders, in my experience, have always been pleasant; one even at least pretends to remember my boyfriend, if not actually remembering him. One time she even took back a beer my friend ended up disliking even after sampling it, even though she was fully prepared to just purchase a new one (The \"Dirty Ho,\" by the way, is very sweet, not for the average beer lover). She gave her a new beer, free of charge. Also ..."},{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","review_id":"RX2NLlpVxwXg3L563NVg3Q","date":"2016-02-11T14:28:25","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9391523599624634,"text_excerpt":"I always like coming here for football or baseball and quick good New Orleans bar food amongst the locals. It's not amazing food or anything but it's perfect for catching the Super Bowl so if you're rating the place on service, atmosphere, and quality bar food, Cooter Brown's scores a five. They had a limited Mardi Gras menu but we were still able to grab a few dozen raw oysters, Gumbo, Jambalaya, and Shrimp Po' Boys. My friend had a Jalapeño Burger and loved it. She even thought it was better than the one at GB Patio. The burger was juicy and had a very unique and delicious melding of spices. Even their Bloody Mary had good spices and nice pickled vegetables. The flavors and crunchiness ..."},{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","review_id":"T-cpgAstMO87w0TdG-7niA","date":"2016-09-15T21:58:46","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.936840295791626,"text_excerpt":"This place is a laid back dive bar with one of the biggest and best beer selections in the entire city. The oyster prices seem a tad high, but they are some of the best oysters in the city and their other items are well priced. This place is a great location to watch sports in a communal type setting too. I really do like that the new owners cleaned up the place, if just a little bit. The only thing that upsets me about this place is their changed up menu. I was really upset they got rid of the soft shelled crab. Also, don't order the poutine. The cheese curds were subpar and the gravy tasted as if it came from a can."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","photo_id":"MIM3vNdmZ6C3qLRYybypgA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/MIM3vNdmZ6C3qLRYybypgA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8421156406402588},{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","photo_id":"zyCvkaDJXId5Abf7BsIZMw","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/zyCvkaDJXId5Abf7BsIZMw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.840223491191864},{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","photo_id":"mZcKwI4EBliEy_RtQDZsmg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/mZcKwI4EBliEy_RtQDZsmg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7759669423103333},{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","photo_id":"l3afhKk3pIFgPx5JNP5yew","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/l3afhKk3pIFgPx5JNP5yew.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7381970882415771},{"business_id":"iJiNZw2TEwB579dr6LyVZQ","photo_id":"XA0ZhsrD4mac3VrXrGr6WQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/XA0ZhsrD4mac3VrXrGr6WQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.734583854675293}]},"notebook_case":null}
